# Rust build artifacts
/target/

# Stores a test or a local run left behind. dc-store's suites write to the
# system temp directory, not here, but `dcstore --db` will happily point at a
# path inside the workspace and a committed lease database would hand every
# checkout someone else's active leases.
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm

# testdata is extractor *input*, not build output.
#
# Same hazard rust-port documents at the bottom of its own ignore file: this
# workspace sits inside a Python repository whose root patterns (`__pycache__`,
# `build/`, `dist/`, `.venv/`) govern anything not re-included here. The fnmatch
# parity fixture is the cross-language gate between this crate and the Go
# matcher, so it must be tracked no matter what the parent ignores.
!testdata/
!testdata/**
